Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||08-17-2000||10:17 PM||||I've also have not seen a 3.1 truck.  I however must question the prudency of a cheap crank.  That is pretty much the heart of the engine.  You sure you want it to be cheap?  I've found that usually one gets what he/she pays for.  <P>My 2 cents<P>Regards||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-18-2000||12:37 AM||||I have never seen a 3.1L in a Truck but I know they were in vans and had iron heads. Could this be what was ment?||||reg||1
Z||000004||HYPTNOTiSE||08-18-2000||07:44 AM||||yeah i wonder if that is what he means, in vans?  Do you mean like the lumina/transport vans? See i dont think those have forged cranks, never heard that they did before.<BR>Astro van maybe?<BR>When i said cheap i meant, cheap as in cheap for a forged crankshaft. Forged cranks cost 1500 new from moldex and i thought it was the only source for a forged crank.  A used crank shouldn't cost more than 100 bucks and then all you need to do is have your machine shop recondition it. I'd take a reconditioned forged crank over a brand spankin new cast crank anyday.<P>My dad mentioned to me that before the 3.4 liter crate engine came out they have a 3.1 liter crate engine.  Maybe this is what he's talking about???||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-18-2000||08:14 AM||||has any one else heard this? Ed 3.5-3.6 can come with forged cranks..!?!?||||reg||1
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||08-18-2000||08:26 AM||||The 3.1 and 3.4 (pushrods) are identical engines except the 3.4 has beefier side walls for a larger bore. same crank and rods and all.<P>-Rick||||reg||1
Z||000007||pollock||08-18-2000||09:24 AM||||AH, YES.......  I know the answer to this one.<P>S-10 trucks and blazers were available in Mexico with 3.1s after the 2.8s went by the wayside.  These must be the forged crank trucks.<P>So, for those of us in Texas, they might not be that hard to get.<P>Hmm... a forged crank would be nice in a heavily NOS'd 3.4.......||||reg||10
